  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">WFP Moldova &#x2013; Emergency aid to crisis-affected populations, supporting social protection reforms and system responsiveness</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Funding is provided to deliver direct support to vulnerable Moldovan households and Ukrainian refugees through bi-monthly cash assistance and daily hot meal provision. This support addresses immediate needs while also strengthening the national social protection system. Focus areas include enhancing the Ajutor Social Programme, digitalising key systems like UAHelp and SIASS, and building shock-responsive capacity through Standard Operating Procedures and contingency planning. The project also supports government staff training and strategic coordination to ensure sustainability, and a responsible WFP exit by 2026.</narrative>
  </description>
